From c4ce39c6b4601bb4fdb8aa3e5f8de8d412fb8348 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 17:00:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(vulkan): choose the host-split memory type by
 measurement, not by index order

The beyond-reservation weight bytes of the 27B S-X8 load are placed in Vulkan
memory type 1 for one reason: the UMA placement chain reaches heap 1 in its
third required-flag pass and the candidate walk returns types in ascending
index. Type 3 - the same heap, the same HOST_COHERENT guarantee, plus
HOST_CACHED - is equally eligible and is already served on this box for the
staging buffers. Nothing has ever measured the two against each other.

Enumeration first (r58-evidence/10-memtypes.txt): every storage buffer reports
memoryTypeBits=0xf, so of 16 enumerated memory types only 0-3 are eligible and
exactly TWO of them lie beyond the reservation. That is the whole lever, and
this commit makes it selectable and measurable.

- test-backend-ops memtype: GPU read GB/s per memory type, timed as an f16
  mat-vec on the ordinary backend so it cannot drift from the served path,
  with the CPU memcpy of the same span beside it. HQ runs it quiet.
- GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MEMTYPE=legacy|<index>|auto and GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_CACHED
  reorder ONLY the host-split candidates of a plan; device-local candidates
  keep their exact position, so a load that fits device memory places exactly
  as before. Default legacy: nothing changes until HQ picks a winner.
- One ungated stderr line per host-split buffer naming type, heap, flags, bytes.

Corrects the lane brief on receipt evidence: output.weight and the DFlash2
recurrent cache are DEVICE-LOCAL, not host-split; heap 0 is 21.07 GiB, not the
16 GiB BIOS carve.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-244 R58 UMA memory-type placement, Opus 5 MEDIUM maker)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED by the maker - placement only, bit-identical (every eligible heap-1 type is HOST_COHERENT, so no flush/invalidate obligation changes); HQ probes every memory type quiet and serves the winner (target: S-X8 27B plain 56 -> ~73 GB/s effective)
Lane: lane-244
Conflict-resolved: S4 split (f172be756): auto_split - our hunks re-homed into ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp; wrap/same-point regions merged in place (fixS4_632.py)
Conflict-resolved: auto: affix(one side only added lines around the base, other side edited it) in tests/test-backend-ops.cpp
