+| `GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MEMTYPE` | **unset = `legacy`, which changes no byte of today's placement.** Accepts `legacy`, a decimal memory **type index**, or `auto`. `auto` reads the probe receipt named by `GGML_VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_FILE` and takes the fastest **non-`DEVICE_LOCAL`** row in it. Anything unparsable, an index out of range, a missing or rowless receipt file: one stderr line and the legacy order stands — it never fails a load. Parsed once per process. Added 2026-09-15 (lane-244/R58). | Scope: the **order of the host-split candidates inside one plan**, in `ggml_backend_vk_buffer_type_plan_begin()`, and nothing else. `DEVICE_LOCAL` candidates keep their exact position, so a load that fits device memory picks precisely what it picked before; a named type that is not a candidate for a buffer leaves that buffer's order untouched. The bound (`GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MAX`), the staging reserve and every ledger check are unchanged and still decide capacity. One stderr line **per host-split buffer**, ungated: `host-split buffer i: N B -> memtype T heap H flags=... (pref=...)`. | Leave unset until HQ has probed. Then set the index the probe crowned, or `auto` with the receipt file. | **UNMEASURED by the maker — placement only, and bit-identical by construction:** every eligible heap-1 type on this box carries `HOST_COHERENT`, so no flush/invalidate obligation changes and the same shader reads the same bytes. **What the enumeration establishes (`r58-evidence/10-memtypes.txt`):** every storage buffer reports `memoryTypeBits=0xf`, so beyond the reservation exactly **two** types are usable — **1** (`HOST_VISIBLE\|HOST_COHERENT`) and **3** (the same plus `HOST_CACHED`) — and today's split lands in type 1 **by ascending index order alone**, never by a measurement. Type 3 is already served on this box for staging (7 allocations, 27,695,584 B), so the driver demonstrably supports it. The number this lane exists to move: S-X8 27B plain decode reads ~56 GB/s effective against ~73 GB/s f