+| `GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_CACHED` | **unset = no opinion (legacy order).** `0` prefers a host-split type **without** `HOST_CACHED`, `1` prefers one **with** it. Ignored whenever `GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MEMTYPE` names an explicit index — that is the more specific instrument. Anything but `0`/`1`: one stderr line, ignored. Added 2026-09-15 (lane-244/R58). | Scope: identical to the row above — the same reorder, selected by the `HOST_CACHED` bit instead of by index. Exists because the enumeration found a genuine cached/uncached pair on this box; on a device offering only one host-visible type it is a no-op and says so by leaving the order alone. | The portable way to ask the question the index asks on this box. Use `=1` against `=0` as a two-arm pairing out of one binary. | **UNMEASURED.** On the 780M `=0` selects type 1 (today's behaviour) and `=1` selects type 3. Which is faster for GPU-side weight reads through GART is exactly the open question — snooped/cached can cost coherence traffic or can win on the read path, and nothing on this rig has measured it. |
+| `GGML_VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_FILE` | **unset = `auto` is unavailable** (it prints one stderr line and falls back to `legacy`). A path to the receipt written by `test-backend-ops memtype`. Added 2026-09-15 (lane-244/R58). | Scope: read only when `GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MEMTYPE=auto`, once per process. The receipt line is emitted and parsed by the same translation unit (`VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_LINE_FMT` / `_SCAN` in `ggml-vulkan.cpp`) so writer and reader cannot drift: `ggml_vulkan memtype-probe v1: type=T heap=H flags=0xF bytes=B gpu_read_gbs=X cpu_memcpy_gbs=Y`. Rows whose flags carry `DEVICE_LOCAL` are reference numbers and are never selected. | Only with `auto`. | **Instrument, no performance claim.** The probe itself (`test-backend-ops memtype [--bytes N] [--rounds R] [--types 1,3]`) times an f16 mat-vec over `N` bytes pinned into one memory type — the same shader path a plain decode token runs — plus the CPU memcpy of the same span. **HQ runs it quiet; the maker never ran it.** |
 | `--spec-draft-adaptive` | **OFF.** CLI flag; sizes each draft from a per-sequence EMA of accepted tokens instead of a fixed `--spec-draft-n-max`, which becomes a safety ceiling rather than a tuning parameter. Backing off is averaged (alpha 0.25, ~4-step memory); probing upward is additive. Reset on `begin()` — a new prompt or a reused server slot — never mid-generation. | Scope: `common/speculative.cpp` draft-length selection. Sits in the `else` of this fork's existing DFlash2 adaptive selector, so a controller already armed keeps precedence; the MTP sites keep their own adaptive precedence. Speculation stays distribution-preserving, so the flag can move throughput and **cannot** move output. | Turn it on where content type varies within a session and no single fixed depth is right — its author's motivating measurement is that the correct depth is *opposite* for prose and for JSON. Sweep it against your own fixed depth before adopting. | **UNMEASURED ON RIG-A — no A/B for this flag exists on this hardware, and none should be quoted.** The measured table in the source commit was taken on a **Radeon 8060S** by the upstream author (three drafter configurations × prose/json × fixed-vs-adaptive, 300 greedy tokens on a Qwen3.8-27B ROCmFP4-FAST target). Those are **upstream-reported numbers for a different GPU** and are deliberately not restated here as results of this fork. Default OFF for that reason alone: the mechanism is sound and the evidence for it is somebody else's box. |
 | `GGML_ARIFI_FA_DEQUANT_KV` | **Device default when unset, which is ON on every device** (upstream behaviour). `1` forces the f16 dequant-KV scratch copy ON, `0` forces the in-place quantized-KV read. Added 2026-09-06 (lane-212/R19), default flipped to ON 2026-09-07 (lane-220/R27). | Scope: Vulkan flash attention with a quantized K and V, prefill only (`neq1 >= 64`); decode never reaches it. One stderr receipt line `ggml_vulkan: FA dequant-KV scratch: ON\|OFF (device default\|GGML_ARIFI_FA_DEQUANT_KV)` binds every A/B log to the path it ran. Bit-identical either way - the same FA math with f32 accumulation, only the KV read strategy differs. A device that measures the scratch copy as a cost flips its own default at `fa_deq_device_default`, with its number. | Leave it unset. Set `0` to reproduce the pre-R27 AMD RDNA3 arm on the same binary, or on a device where the scratch copy is measurably a cost. | **The knob and the receipt are the result; the magnitude is NOT.** R19D measured `+8.08%` clean prefill on one binary and R27 flipped the default on it. The R18 wave recomputed the same banked rounds on 2026-09-08 and **it does not reproduce**: gate OFF vs ON on one binary reads decode `+0.49%` CI95 `[-1.62%, +2.59%]` and prefill `+0.85%` `[+0.36%, +1.33%]`; the DFlash2 arm reads decode `-0.91%` `[-1.93%, +0.12%]`. Do not quote `+8.08%`. Evidence: `research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-09-02-lane-209/r18-kernel-wave/R18-KERNEL-WAVE-REPORT.md`, `.../r19-seat-prefill/R19D-ENGAGEMENT-LEGS.md`. |
 | `LLAMA_DFLASH_FUSED_INJECT` | **OFF when unset on this fork - the LEGACY encode+decode path. This DIVERGES from upstream 662a0b012, deliberately.** `1` selects the fused injection (upstream shape). Added 2026-09-06 (lane-212/R18), default set to legacy 2026-09-08 (lane-225/R38). The C API default (`llama_cparams::dflash_fused_inject`) stays **fused**, because the legacy shape is a caller contract - the caller must `llama_encode` the chunk first - so only `common/speculative.cpp`, which owns both halves, defaults it off. | Scope: the DFlash2 drafter's K/V injection only. Fused = one `llama_decode` per chunk with the encoder (fc + rms norm) in-graph. Legacy = `llama_encode` the chunk through `graph<true>`, read the encoded rows back through `llama_get_embeddings_nextn`, feed them to the injection decode at the draft width. Nothing removed: `graph<true>`, the fused embd branch and the legacy host path all stay compiled. One receipt line per process names the arm. | Set `1` to restore upstream behaviour, and on any box that has not measured this pair. The default here is a **conservative choice on a sub-floor number, not a measured win** - see the cost cell before treating it as a recommendation. | **DOCUMENTED-TAKE, no gain, and the default flip is under the floor.** Seat DFlash2 decode `-0.98%` CI95 `[-1.16%, -0.80%]` fused vs legacy; U-IQ4XS `+0.05%` `[-0.56%, +0.67%]`; U-Q3KXL `-0.87%` `[-2.50%, +0.77%]`. Against this box's own build floor - the R18 wave's INERT controls, where both arms ran identical code, moved decode by up to **+3.71%** and prefill by up to **-8.28%**, both excluding zero, so **none of these three clears it** and the direction is all the flip rests on. Quality: F-141 both arms on the seat, `test-quantize-fns` identical to the bank. Evidence: `.../r18-kernel-wave/r15c2-dflash-encoder-fusion`. |
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp
index 4afe0ef1dd..c4439e0ac1 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp
@@ -96,6 +96,135 @@ static const char * ggml_vk_plan_entry_name(const char * const * names, size_t i
 // now receives each buffer's first tensor name, the host-placement receipt says WHICH buffers went
 // to the host mapping instead of only how many bytes, and GGML_VK_ALLOC_TRACE dumps the whole plan.
 //
+// R58 lane-244 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// WHICH MEMORY TYPE the beyond-reservation (host-split) weight bytes come from.
+//
+// Enumeration on this box (r58-evidence/10-memtypes.txt, and the R51 alloc trace
+// r51-evidence/30-planorder.txt): every storage buffer we create reports memoryTypeBits=0xf, so
+// only memory types 0-3 are eligible at all. Two of those four live on the non-DEVICE_LOCAL heap
+// 1: type 1 (HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT) and type 3 (the same plus HOST_CACHED). The UMA placement
+// chain reaches heap 1 only in its third required-flag pass ({HV|HC}), and
+// ggml_vk_find_memory_properties() returns candidates in ASCENDING TYPE INDEX, so type 1 wins by
+// enumeration order alone - it has never been chosen by a measurement. These switches let a
+// measured choice replace that accident.
+//
+// GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MEMTYPE = legacy (default, nothing changes) | <index> | auto
+// GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_CACHED  = 0 | 1   (prefer a host-split type without / with HOST_CACHED)
+// GGML_VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_FILE = receipt file `auto` reads (written by `test-backend-ops memtype`)
+//
+// Both only ever REORDER the host-split candidates of a plan. Device-local candidates keep their
+// exact position, so a load that fits device memory picks precisely what it picked before, and a
+// preference that cannot be satisfied falls through to the legacy order instead of failing the
+// load (same principle as the bulk-large-heap fallback below).
+#define VK_HOST_SPLIT_LEGACY (-1)
+#define VK_HOST_SPLIT_AUTO   (-2)
+
+// The ONE definition of the probe receipt line: ggml_vk_memtype_probe_line() writes it and
+// ggml_vk_host_split_auto_type() parses it. Two hand-kept copies in different translation units
+// would drift and `auto` would silently stop finding the winner.
+#define VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_LINE_PREFIX "ggml_vulkan memtype-probe v1:"
+#define VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_LINE_FMT \
+    VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_LINE_PREFIX " type=%u heap=%u flags=0x%x bytes=%llu gpu_read_gbs=%.3f cpu_memcpy_gbs=%.3f\n"
+#define VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_LINE_SCAN \
+    VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_LINE_PREFIX " type=%u heap=%u flags=0x%x bytes=%llu gpu_read_gbs=%lf cpu_memcpy_gbs=%lf"
+
+// Reads the probe receipt and returns the FASTEST non-DEVICE_LOCAL memory type in it, or
+// VK_HOST_SPLIT_LEGACY when the file is absent, unreadable or carries no such row. Refusing the
+// load instead would turn a missing receipt into a broken engine.
+static int ggml_vk_host_split_auto_type() {
+    const char * path = getenv("GGML_VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_FILE");
+    if (path == nullptr || *path == '\0') {
+        fprintf(stderr, "ggml_vulkan: GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MEMTYPE=auto but GGML_VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_FILE "
+                        "is unset; falling back to the legacy placement order\n");
+        return VK_HOST_SPLIT_LEGACY;
+    }
+    FILE * f = fopen(path, "r");
+    if (f == nullptr) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "ggml_vulkan: GGML_VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_FILE '%s' cannot be read; falling back to "
+                        "the legacy placement order\n", path);
+        return VK_HOST_SPLIT_LEGACY;
+    }
+    int    best_type = VK_HOST_SPLIT_LEGACY;
+    double best_gbs  = -1.0;
+    char   line[512];
+    while (fgets(line, sizeof(line), f) != nullptr) {
+        unsigned int       type = 0, heap = 0, flags = 0;
+        unsigned long long bytes = 0;
+        double             gpu_gbs = 0.0, cpu_gbs = 0.0;
+        if (sscanf(line, VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_LINE_SCAN, &type, &heap, &flags, &bytes, &gpu_gbs, &cpu_gbs) != 6) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        // Only the beyond-reservation types are candidates: a DEVICE_LOCAL row in the receipt is
+        // the reference number, not something the host split may be pointed at.
+        if (flags & (unsigned int) VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_DEVICE_LOCAL_BIT) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        if (gpu_gbs > best_gbs) {
+            best_gbs  = gpu_gbs;
+            best_type = (int) type;
+        }
+    }
+    fclose(f);
+    if (best_type == VK_HOST_SPLIT_LEGACY) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "ggml_vulkan: GGML_VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_FILE '%s' has no host-visible probe row; "
+                        "falling back to the legacy placement order\n", path);
+    } else {
+        fprintf(stderr, "ggml_vulkan: host-split memory type auto -> %d (%.3f GB/s in %s)\n",
+                best_type, best_gbs, path);
+    }
+    return best_type;
+}
+
+// Parsed ONCE per process. getenv() on a per-buffer path would be called thousands of times in a
+// load, and `auto` would re-read and re-print the receipt file for every buffer.
+static int ggml_vk_host_split_memtype() {
+    static const int pref = [] {
+        const char * s = getenv("GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MEMTYPE");
+        if (s == nullptr || *s == '\0' || strcmp(s, "legacy") == 0) {
+            return (int) VK_HOST_SPLIT_LEGACY;
+        }
+        if (strcmp(s, "auto") == 0) {
+            return ggml_vk_host_split_auto_type();
+        }
+        char * end = nullptr;
+        errno = 0;
+        const long v = strtol(s, &end, 10);
+        if (errno != 0 || end == s || *end != '\0' || v < 0 || v >= (long) VK_MAX_MEMORY_TYPES) {
+            fprintf(stderr, "ggml_vulkan: GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MEMTYPE='%s' is not legacy|auto|<index>; "
+                            "keeping the legacy placement order\n", s);
+            return (int) VK_HOST_SPLIT_LEGACY;
+        }
+        return (int) v;
+    }();
+    return pref;
+}
+
+// -1 = unset (no opinion), 0 = prefer a host-split type WITHOUT HOST_CACHED, 1 = prefer one WITH
+// it. Only consulted when GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MEMTYPE names no explicit index.
+static int ggml_vk_host_split_cached() {
+    static const int want = [] {
+        const char * s = getenv("GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_CACHED");
+        if (s == nullptr || *s == '\0') {
+            return -1;
+        }
+        if (strcmp(s, "0") == 0) {
+            return 0;
+        }
+        if (strcmp(s, "1") == 0) {
+            return 1;
+        }
+        fprintf(stderr, "ggml_vulkan: GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_CACHED='%s' is not 0|1; ignored\n", s);
+        return -1;
+    }();
+    return want;
+}
+
+// R58 lane-244: PROBE-ONLY memory type pin, written solely by ggml_vk_memtype_force() (the
+// bandwidth probe in test-backend-ops). While set, ggml_vk_find_memory_properties() admits exactly
+// one memory type index, so a probe allocation comes from that type or does not happen at all.
+// Nothing in a model load ever writes this; it is -1 for the whole life of a served process.
+static std::atomic<int> vk_memtype_forced{-1};
+
 // The reserve is sized from a real requirement, not a guess: a bulk weight buffer is capped at
 // suballocation_block_size (ggml_backend_vk_buffer_type_get_max_size), one tensor lives inside one
